    "about": "The front end’s cameras as the game moves them (bf2-re findings/53): each screen requests a camera by name (UICameraRequestState); the PF_UI_CameraLocator of that name in Levels/Frontend/Camera writes UIActiveCameraState (its transform, FocusDistance, Aperture, whether the character shows: the LevelData’s interface constants); Camera_Schematic moves the camera entity there with a TransformInterpolator (Expo, ease-out, 1 s between these screens) and sets its FocalLength through PF_UI_CameraFocalLength (50 mm at 16:9) on the CamBody_Cine sensor. Positions are the game’s world: the stage frame is the world less origin (Backdrop_01’s dome); pivot is where the character stands (the Camera layer’s inspect locator). A camera looks down −forward. The collection’s cameras follow the character’s bones and are left out. HOME has a locator for each UICharacterKitSize but Normal (home.Small, home.Tall, home.ExtraTall: Camera_Schematic enables one by the character’s KitSize), and each kit stands at the pivot moved by its KitUIMetaData CustomizationTransform (kits).",
